      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How often do I need to update my Safety Data Sheets?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "REACH Article 31(9) requires that an SDS is updated without delay whenever new information becomes available that may affect risk management measures or the hazard information, or if a REACH authorisation or restriction has been granted or refused for the substance. Additionally, SDSs must be updated whenever a substance is included in the SVHC Candidate List (at concentrations above 0.1% w/w), when there is a new CLP harmonised classification, and when the regulatory status of ingredients changes. In practice, lubricant manufacturers should review their SDS portfolio at minimum annually against the latest ECHA Candidate List updates (published approximately twice yearly), any new harmonised classifications, and any REACH Annex XVII restriction entries. All downstream customers who have received the SDS in the previous 12 months must be supplied with the revised version." }
